miadi-chronicle-client — the Miadi chronicle's commands and MCP servers

  sudo apt install miadi-chronicle-client

The client half: what an agent or a person runs on any machine to read,
relate and write the chronicle through the Miadi API. Each command is a
pinned npm release under /usr/lib/miadi-chronicle-client, run by miadi-node:

  inquiry-weave        episodes, relations, the chronicle catalog (@miadi/inquiry-weave)
  inquiry-weave-mcp    the same as an MCP server
  passages, mkepisode  episode vessels (passages)
  miadi-voice-mcp      voice for an episode, as an MCP server (@miadi/voice-mcp)
  medicine-wheel-mcp   the chronicle wheel, as an MCP server (@medicine-wheel/mcp)

The MCP servers are the ones the miadi-chronicle-episode-kit Claude Code
plugin runs with npx, at the same versions. An MCP config can name the
command instead: "command": "/usr/bin/miadi-voice-mcp", with the same env.
That needs no npm cache and no network when a session starts.

They read the same settings as their npm form (MIADI_API_URL,
MIADI_API_TOKEN_WRITER, MIADI_CHRONICLE_MW_URL, ...), from the environment;
miadi-config holds the host's values.

SOURCE lists each pinned package and the resolved tree. A user's own npm
install (nvm, /usr/local) comes first on PATH and wins over /usr/bin.

Source: https://github.com/jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit, packages/miadi/deb
Pins:   prep/miadi-chronicle-client.packages (jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit#77)
